{"id": "EUVD-2026-102524", "enisaUuid": "bc927943-f98a-375a-8671-2dc9169e3f68", "description": "libical through 4.0.6 contains a heap-based out-of-bounds read in icalvalue_decode_ical_string() in src/libical/icalvalue.c when decoding input ending in a backslash. Attackers can supply escaped iCalendar text with a trailing backslash, causing the loop to read past the terminator and crash the application or leak adjacent heap memory.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T21:43:16", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libical-icalvalue-decode-ical-string-oob-read", "https://github.com/libical/libical/pull/1455", "https://github.com/libical/libical/commit/d753885ce2de7c105d6b8c405aa7aee1d98ad8de", "https://github.com/libical/libical/blob/9cfca65c122fa23b9680a28e0c9225a2fd015fc5/src/libical/icalvalue.c#L1608-L1645", "https://github.com/libical/libical", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libical-through-4.0.6-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-icalvalue-decode-ical-string"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111269", "GHSA-qvfg-9jj8-868q"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "acc3d431-c19f-3ca8-a9c2-0746e0290b66", "product": {"name": "libical", "vendor": {"name": "libical"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.0.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0c987d2e-023d-3c37-98ab-2a03f3003f09", "vendor": {"name": "libical"}}], "isExploited": false}